 {
  "skill": "fn-limit-concept",
  "problems": [
   {
    "question": "$f(x) = \\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3}$, where $x \\neq 3$.\nBy investigating the values of $f(x)$ for $x$ close to $3$, find the limiting value of $f(x)$ as $x \\to 3$.",
    "level": "ordinary",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Simplify the function for $x \\neq 3$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "\\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3} &= \\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3}",
         "sym": "(x**2 - 9)/(x - 3)"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= x + 3",
         "sym": "x + 3"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Try values just below and just above 3",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "f(2.99) &= 2.99 + 3 = 5.99",
         "sym": "Eq(Rational(299,100) + 3, Rational(599,100))",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "f(3.01) &= 3.01 + 3 = 6.01",
         "sym": "Eq(Rational(301,100) + 3, Rational(601,100))",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "State the limiting value",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "From both sides, $f(x)$ gets closer and closer to $6$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "\\lim_{x \\to 3} f(x) &= 3 + 3 = 6",
         "sym": "Eq(limit(x + 3, x, 3), 6)",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "6"
    },
    "finalSym": "6",
    "answerSym": "limit((x**2 - 9)/(x - 3), x, 3)"
   },
   {
    "question": "The temperature of a drink $t$ minutes after it is poured is $T(t) = 5 + 40e^{-0.2t}$ °C.\nFind the temperature that $T(t)$ approaches as $t$ gets very large.",
